# Line endings. Every file written through the Windows mount comes back as CRLF,
# so without this git reports every line of every text file as changed. On
# 2026-10-15 the working tree showed 2546 insertions against 2546 deletions with
# zero content difference (`git diff --ignore-all-space` was empty).
#
# text=auto  git stores LF in the repository and decides text vs binary itself,
#            so images and fonts are untouched.
# eol=crlf   the working tree is CRLF on every machine, Windows and the Linux
#            mount alike, so the two never disagree about what "unchanged" means.
#
# After adding this file, run `git add --renormalize .` ON WINDOWS once and commit.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Shell scripts genuinely break with CRLF (the shebang line). Nothing else here does.
*.sh text eol=lf
